-- title:
--   Bounds for truncated Chebyshev expansions
-- statement:
--   Let $Q=\sum_{j=0}^nc_jT_j$ be a Chebyshev expansion with $|Q(x)|\le M$ for all $x\in[-1,1]$, where $M\ge0$. Then for every $d$ and every $x\in[-1,1]$,
--   $$
--   \Bigl|\sum_{j\le d}c_jT_j(x)\Bigr|\le2M(d+1).
--   $$
--
--   Keeping only the low Chebyshev modes costs at most a factor $2(d+1)$ in the sup norm on $[-1,1]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/ChebyshevTruncation.lean#L25-L44

